1
00:00:02,660 --> 00:00:06,457
It looks like no one in Koichi's
family knows where he went either.

2
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:09,217
And from the sound of things,
they're close to calling the police.

3
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:11,182
Dammit, so he really is missing.

4
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:13,657
Yukako is nowhere to be seen either.

5
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:15,540
I feel like it's all my fault.

6
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:17,010
Wait!

7
00:00:17,093 --> 00:00:19,537
You don't think she snapped
and snuffed him out, do you?

8
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:20,450
Well, no.

9
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:22,217
I don't think it's come to that.

10
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:24,535
Regardless, she's holding him captive.

11
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:27,017
Come on, we need to
find him and do it fast.

12
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:31,218
I feel like we don't have much time
left if we want to find him alive.

13
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:34,860
It won't open!

14
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:36,960
This can't be happening to me!

15
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:40,530
Damn,

16
00:00:40,613 --> 00:00:43,077
I'm pretty sure there was a
movie that has the answer I need,

17
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:46,925
but I never ended up watching it
because it looked way too long!

18
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:50,777
I think I've almost got this
ridiculous thing figured out.

19
00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:56,540
One, and then four, zero, zero, open!

20
00:02:25,900 --> 00:02:29,520
I washed your pajama bottoms,
as well as your underwear.

21
00:02:32,940 --> 00:02:34,160
Is there a problem?

22
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:38,640
I can't help if I don't know what's wrong.

23
00:02:39,820 --> 00:02:42,377
It's just that I'm a
freshman in high school.

24
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:44,420
How could I let this happen?

25
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:50,009
I'd be embarrassed if I didn't already
feel like a pathetic waste of a human.

26
00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:51,530
Enough.

27
00:02:51,613 --> 00:02:53,080
Please, stop this.

28
00:02:53,780 --> 00:02:56,540
I mean, surely you must despise me by now.

29
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:58,120
Don't I disgust you?

30
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:01,620
Won't you please just let me go home now?

31
00:03:01,820 --> 00:03:05,644
What could you possibly like about
a guy who just peed his pants?

32
00:03:06,760 --> 00:03:09,540
Koichi, you poor pitiful thing. How awful.

33
00:03:09,740 --> 00:03:13,152
I must be putting your gentle
heart through so much agony.

34
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,580
I'm such a bad girl,
the lowest of the low.

35
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:19,057
Nothing I say has any effect on her.

36
00:03:19,140 --> 00:03:20,980
I think I'm gonna cry.

37
00:03:21,340 --> 00:03:23,660
First I wet myself, now this.

38
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:26,040
What the hell is going on?

39
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:28,520
There's just one thing.

40
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:32,077
I was watching when you
talked about being a pathetic

41
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:35,560
human being and saw a sparkle
deep behind your eyes.

42
00:03:35,820 --> 00:03:39,160
What I saw in that moment
was positively intoxicating.

43
00:03:39,780 --> 00:03:44,309
If I didn't know any better, I'd swear
you were hiding an ace up your sleeve.

44
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:49,700
And if I'm being honest, it
makes me like you even more.

45
00:03:50,020 --> 00:03:53,138
It's the reason I want to
learn everything about you.

46
00:03:53,820 --> 00:03:54,650
After all,

47
00:03:54,733 --> 00:03:58,277
what's a little bit of poop and snot when
you're madly in love with your soulmate?

48
00:03:58,360 --> 00:03:59,190
Right, Ko?

49
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:01,097
I'm surprised you were worried.

50
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:03,017
Washing your soiled unmentionables filled

51
00:04:03,100 --> 00:04:05,629
me with a kind of joy
that I'd never known.

52
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:10,150
Look!

53
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:13,600
What do you think?

54
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:15,546
I'm making an electric chair.

55
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:19,112
With any luck, it'll be ready
for our dinner time studies.

56
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:27,108
I was thinking about trying out
a new Italian recipe tonight.

57
00:04:27,280 --> 00:04:29,339
So I have to stock up on olive oil.

58
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,260
I can't wait.

59
00:04:37,140 --> 00:04:38,460
Somebody help me!

60
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:41,997
She's going further and
further off the deep end!

61
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:43,677
I have to get out of here faster!

62
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:45,701
She's seriously going to kill me!

63
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:48,670
But...

64
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:52,800
How exactly do I do that?

65
00:04:57,260 --> 00:04:59,577
I might be completely wrong about this?

66
00:04:59,660 --> 00:05:02,237
But even if someone's found
a way to keep Koichi quiet,

67
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:04,908
can he still call out
for help using Reverb?

68
00:05:05,380 --> 00:05:08,968
Ideally, yes, but Reverb only
has a range of about 50 meters.

69
00:05:09,300 --> 00:05:12,677
If he was taken somewhere isolated,
his powers would be no good.

70
00:05:12,760 --> 00:05:15,407
It's like looking for
a needle in a haystack.

71
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:18,510
Hang on.

72
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:21,835
She said something about
stocking up on more olive oil.

73
00:05:22,420 --> 00:05:24,891
But she wouldn't go shopping at this hour.

74
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:27,162
Maybe she's doing a phone order?

75
00:05:29,780 --> 00:05:31,360
Hey, could it be?

76
00:05:36,860 --> 00:05:38,760
It is! A payphone!

77
00:05:39,860 --> 00:05:41,620
I'm 48 meters away!

78
00:05:41,940 --> 00:05:43,940
Yes, it's just within range!

79
00:05:45,940 --> 00:05:48,340
Thank goodness Reverb is a soundstand!

80
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:51,111
Now I can signal Josuke and get some help!

81
00:05:53,860 --> 00:05:56,480
I don't have any 10 yen coins!

82
00:05:58,040 --> 00:05:58,870
planes!

83
00:05:58,953 --> 00:06:00,777
I was in my pajamas
when I was dragged here!

84
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:02,277
Should I just dial 110?

85
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:06,100
But if I do that, she might
kill the officers! Damn it!

86
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:09,097
I'll just have to find some
other way to contact Josuke!

87
00:06:09,180 --> 00:06:13,651
You were wondering whether there was a
payphone nearby, weren't you, Koichi?

88
00:06:15,900 --> 00:06:16,780
Yukako!

89
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:18,597
You don't have to pretend.

90
00:06:18,680 --> 00:06:20,537
I know precisely what you're thinking.

91
00:06:20,620 --> 00:06:23,337
Since I told you that I was
going to go buy some olive oil,

92
00:06:23,420 --> 00:06:25,157
you thought there must
be a payphone nearby.

93
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:28,600
but it needed 10 yen coins,
which you don't have.

94
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:30,351
Does that about cover it?

95
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:33,500
Oh, there's a payphone? How about that?

96
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:35,838
Feigning ignorance?

97
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:39,259
I give up on the notion of
calling someone for help.

98
00:06:39,420 --> 00:06:42,817
You're not taking a single step
outside this house until I say so.

99
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:47,547
But so you won't be tempted, I'm going
to destroy the phone's emergency button.

100
00:06:48,440 --> 00:06:49,940
Would you like anything?

101
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:52,080
No, I guess not.

102
00:06:56,860 --> 00:06:58,920
There's just no reasoning with her.

103
00:06:59,840 --> 00:07:00,980
That was it.

104
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:03,240
My last shot at getting help.

105
00:07:13,420 --> 00:07:15,420
What is this writing?

106
00:07:18,340 --> 00:07:20,811
Why are there sounds coming out of my arm?

107
00:07:22,440 --> 00:07:24,360
The phone's calling someone.

108
00:07:25,020 --> 00:07:26,157
That doesn't make sense.

109
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:27,652
I never dialed a number.

110
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:31,155
Higashikata speaking.

111
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:33,100
I got through!

112
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:37,576
If the right signals are transmitted,
a push-button phone will connect!

113
00:07:37,860 --> 00:07:38,690
Koichi!

114
00:07:38,773 --> 00:07:39,720
Hey, is that you?

115
00:07:39,940 --> 00:07:41,220
It's me, Josuke!

116
00:07:41,740 --> 00:07:43,060
Koichi, where are you?

117
00:07:43,760 --> 00:07:44,590
What's that?

118
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:46,060
I hear waves crashing.

119
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:49,730
Koichi!

120
00:07:49,813 --> 00:07:50,643
Koichi?

121
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:54,620
So I was right, you do
have a power like me.

122
00:07:55,940 --> 00:07:56,960
Yes, I did it!

123
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:59,717
Now Chosuke's gonna rush over
here and rescue me for sure.

124
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:01,800
It'll take 20 minutes tops by car.

125
00:08:01,940 --> 00:08:05,940
I just have to figure out a way to
hold out until they can get here.

126
00:08:07,440 --> 00:08:10,140
A payphone and the sound of waves.

127
00:08:11,780 --> 00:08:14,960
The only place Koichi
could be is right here.

128
00:08:18,120 --> 00:08:18,950
Koichi.

129
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:21,390
Koichi!

130
00:08:21,820 --> 00:08:23,517
She's coming back to the house!

131
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:26,012
Looks like I have no choice but to fight!

132
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:41,300
Open this door, Koichi!

133
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:44,817
You want in so bad, why
don't you break it down?

134
00:08:44,900 --> 00:08:48,606
A broken door will definitely
make Josuke stop and take notice.

135
00:08:53,780 --> 00:08:56,020
You've made me very happy, Koichi.

136
00:08:58,040 --> 00:08:59,937
Discovering you have
powers like I do is the

137
00:09:00,020 --> 00:09:02,726
most wonderful surprise
I could have received.

138
00:09:03,160 --> 00:09:06,657
Though I have to say I'm a bit
irritated that you kept this a secret.

139
00:09:06,740 --> 00:09:08,740
Even so, I'm happy you're like me.

140
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:12,577
Because when a man and a woman decide to
spend the rest of their lives together,

141
00:09:12,660 --> 00:09:15,477
nothing is more important than
a relationship built on love,

142
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:17,037
trust, and shared values, right?

143
00:09:17,120 --> 00:09:22,037
The two of us share something no one else
could ever dream of having think about it.

144
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:23,920
We could be the perfect couple

145
00:09:25,420 --> 00:09:28,400
So please Koichi open the door?

146
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:37,500
When I say open the door
open the goddamn door!

147
00:09:52,560 --> 00:09:54,977
Did you actually believe
we'd be the perfect couple?

148
00:09:55,060 --> 00:09:57,837
Why can't you understand how
much I hate what you're doing?

149
00:09:57,920 --> 00:09:59,897
That noise will keep
bombarding you until you

150
00:09:59,980 --> 00:10:02,717
renounce your love for me
and cry for forgiveness!

151
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:03,630
I hate you!

152
00:10:06,220 --> 00:10:07,050
I hate you!

153
00:10:07,133 --> 00:10:07,963
I hate you!

154
00:10:08,046 --> 00:10:08,876
You're not making sense.

155
00:10:08,959 --> 00:10:11,117
This foolishness is
practically inaudible to me.

156
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:12,960
I hate you! No!

157
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:17,260
What's going on?

158
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:20,037
This isn't at all like
what happened with Tamami.

159
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:21,826
Her delusions are too strong.

160
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:25,318
But I didn't think it'd be
completely useless on her.

161
00:10:28,340 --> 00:10:32,217
I finally found the one person I'm
bound to with the red thread of fate,

162
00:10:32,300 --> 00:10:34,677
and I won't let anything come between us.

163
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:37,080
Some people never find their soulmate.

164
00:10:37,360 --> 00:10:39,700
Don't you understand how lucky we are?

165
00:10:45,900 --> 00:10:49,640
Oh, Koichi, my plan was to turn
you into an outstanding man,

166
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:52,737
but recent events have
forced me to change my mind.

167
00:10:52,820 --> 00:10:56,777
So until you fall madly in love with
me, you will remain in this house.

168
00:10:56,860 --> 00:10:59,620
And make no mistake, you
are going to love me!

169
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:01,400
Or else...

170
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:04,620
I might murder you.

171
00:11:05,820 --> 00:11:08,480
I can't let her in here, no matter what!

172
00:11:08,820 --> 00:11:11,037
I just need to land one
more attack with Reverb!

173
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:14,767
If I go all out, I'll be able
to unleash an even louder sound.

174
00:11:15,420 --> 00:11:16,250
Reverb!

175
00:11:23,040 --> 00:11:24,537
Something's wrong with Reverb.

176
00:11:24,620 --> 00:11:25,679
Are you all right?

177
00:11:27,320 --> 00:11:28,440
He's not moving!

178
00:11:30,400 --> 00:11:32,380
No, what's happening to him?

179
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:36,504
Did he collapse because he sensed
that our situation is hopeless?

180
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:38,657
You're kidding me!

181
00:11:38,740 --> 00:11:40,800
REVERB IS DEAD!

182
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:49,640
What happened?

183
00:11:50,140 --> 00:11:51,720
No, Reverb.

184
00:11:51,900 --> 00:11:55,340
He's been turned into a
lifeless husk! But how?

185
00:11:58,220 --> 00:12:00,500
A stanza manifestation of the soul!

186
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:03,217
Which means I must have
pushed mine too far past

187
00:12:03,300 --> 00:12:06,359
its breaking point and
collapsed under the pressure!

188
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:08,190
Ah!

189
00:12:08,273 --> 00:12:10,252
I didn't mean for this to happen, Reverb!

190
00:12:10,900 --> 00:12:11,730
What?

191
00:12:12,700 --> 00:12:14,677
What the hell did he call that thing?

192
00:12:14,760 --> 00:12:15,620
A stand?

193
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:18,080
Whatever it is, I have to stop it!

194
00:12:19,860 --> 00:12:21,720
Get this thing out of my way!

195
00:12:22,620 --> 00:12:24,080
She's gonna kill me!

196
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:28,889
If that psycho makes it through the door
and catches me, I'm as good as dead!

197
00:12:36,240 --> 00:12:37,820
Koichi, open this door!

198
00:12:39,660 --> 00:12:42,484
I have to stop her from
getting in here somehow!

199
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:46,391
If only there was a way for
that door to blow her far away!

200
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:51,089
It broke out of its shell!

201
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:52,695
Where did you put it?

202
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:55,257
Answer the damn question, Koichi!

203
00:12:55,340 --> 00:12:57,046
Where did you put that thing?

204
00:13:01,020 --> 00:13:01,850
What?

205
00:13:01,933 --> 00:13:02,763
Wait, is that...

206
00:13:02,846 --> 00:13:05,060
I don't believe it! It's reverb!

207
00:13:06,800 --> 00:13:08,000
It's still alive!

208
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:11,697
It must have been changing into a
new form while it was in that shell!

209
00:13:11,780 --> 00:13:12,960
Is this a joke?

210
00:13:13,180 --> 00:13:17,457
Its design hasn't really changed at
all, besides the fact that it shrunk.

211
00:13:17,540 --> 00:13:20,305
Regardless, changing
shape isn't going to help.

212
00:13:20,580 --> 00:13:22,140
Oh man, it's fast!

213
00:13:25,760 --> 00:13:28,120
Where's this wind coming from?

214
00:13:30,380 --> 00:13:31,210
Whoa!

215
00:13:31,293 --> 00:13:32,689
It actually blew her away!

216
00:13:32,960 --> 00:13:37,019
I don't know how, but some kind of
wind blasted her out of the house!

217
00:13:41,200 --> 00:13:43,060
Damn, what just happened to me?

218
00:13:43,300 --> 00:13:44,760
What did that stand do?

219
00:13:46,440 --> 00:13:47,270
Is that?

220
00:13:47,820 --> 00:13:49,960
Yeah, it's Reverb's writing.

221
00:13:54,600 --> 00:13:55,660
I get it now.

222
00:13:55,860 --> 00:13:58,577
She touched the graffiti door
and the writing became real.

223
00:13:58,660 --> 00:14:03,200
The sensation of the word Fish literally
sent her flying. Wait a minute.

224
00:14:03,460 --> 00:14:06,337
Right before it happened,
I wish the door would open.

225
00:14:06,420 --> 00:14:07,250
blow her away.

226
00:14:07,340 --> 00:14:10,057
I didn't realize it, but I was
controlling that sensation.

227
00:14:10,140 --> 00:14:11,200
This is the brand

228
00:14:12,020 --> 00:14:12,850
new Reverb.

229
00:14:12,933 --> 00:14:13,920
Reverb Act Two!

230
00:14:17,700 --> 00:14:18,720
Oh, Koichi.

231
00:14:24,260 --> 00:14:25,160
It's them.

232
00:14:26,820 --> 00:14:29,397
This vacation spot is the one place I know

233
00:14:29,480 --> 00:14:31,497
that's by the sea and
has lots of empty houses.

234
00:14:31,580 --> 00:14:33,360
Yeah, that's great and all.

235
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:35,977
But there are still tons
of houses around here.

236
00:14:36,060 --> 00:14:37,897
How do we find out which one he's in?

237
00:14:37,980 --> 00:14:39,437
By finding the phone booth.

238
00:14:39,520 --> 00:14:42,285
Koichi did call us using
a public phone, right?

239
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:47,600
Once we find that booth, we'll start
searching the nearby houses one by one. Right.

240
00:14:49,920 --> 00:14:53,780
Search around all you want, sweet,
adorable Koichi belongs to me.

241
00:14:54,980 --> 00:14:57,300
I'll never let anyone else have him.

242
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:08,341
I strongly suggest you
keep your distance, Yukako.

243
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:13,037
And you should believe me when I tell you?

244
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:15,157
There's just no way that
your powers can compete.

245
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:17,122
with Rebervac 2's new abilities.

246
00:15:17,560 --> 00:15:19,660
Our days of playing house are over.

247
00:15:24,080 --> 00:15:26,220
Now my left eyelid is twitching.

248
00:15:26,460 --> 00:15:30,800
Since I was a kid, getting upset
always set off my orbicularis oculi.

249
00:15:31,580 --> 00:15:34,237
It was like a weird chick that
said I was about to get violent!

250
00:15:34,320 --> 00:15:35,757
Oh, and just so you know,

251
00:15:35,840 --> 00:15:39,157
one stupid little modification
doesn't suddenly make you a big shot!

252
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:41,652
I'm gonna have to get a little rough now!

253
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:45,680
Ah! Damn it!

254
00:15:45,820 --> 00:15:47,114
How could you do this?

255
